+++ b/extensions/facetime/README.md
@@ -45,6 +45,21 @@ released.
 
 ## Configuration
 
+Set `realtime.mode: "talk"` to use the same conversation, provider, voice,
+instructions, reasoning, tools, and permissions as the OpenClaw app. This mode
+requires a host with the shared Talk carrier runtime. Configure only the
+carrier's owner handles and optional Talk session key; provider, model, voice,
+instruction, and tool-policy overrides belong in Talk configuration.
+
+Normal hangup stops audio and closes call resources, while accepted agent work
+follows native Talk completion into the shared conversation. Explicit task
+cancellation remains separate. Clear commands such as "hang up" or "end this
+call" request native hangup without cancelling accepted work.
+
+The default `realtime.mode: "standalone"` preserves the published carrier
+configuration described below. It does not provide the shared Talk behavior.
+
+
 `ownerHandles` is the only caller list. Every accepted identity receives owner
 authority. `realtime.toolPolicy` is one of `safe-read-only`, `owner`, or `none`;
 invalid explicit values fail validation.
